{title: When the Saints Go Marching In}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - hearing the return home}
{artist: Traditional African American spiritual}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}
{tag: beginner, spiritual, singalong, three chords}
# Traditional public-domain spiritual, not the different 1896 hymn.
# Selected traditional verses; fresh simple accompaniment, no recorded arrangement copied.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Sing the opening "Oh, when the" as a pickup before the first full bar.}
{comment: Listen for G7 leading back to C. Play straight before trying a gentle swing.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching in,
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching [G7]in,
Lord, I [C]want to [F]be in that [C]number,
When the [C]saints go [G7]marching [C]in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh, when the [C]sun refused to shine,
Oh, when the [C]sun refused to [G7]shine,
Lord, I [C]want to [F]be in that [C]number,
When the [C]sun re[G7]fused to [C]shine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Oh, when they [C]crown Him Lord of all,
Oh, when they [C]crown Him Lord of [G7]all,
Lord, I [C]want to [F]be in that [C]number,
When they [C]crown Him [G7]Lord of [C]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Closing verse}
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching in,
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching [G7]in,
Lord, I [C]want to [F]be in that [C]number,
When the [C]saints go [G7]marching [C]in.
{end_of_verse}
